rload due to repeated blood transfusions or iron supplementation.", "ESTEATOPATÍA NO ALCOHÓLICA:Esteatopatía no alcohólica refers to non-alcoholic fatty liver disease, which can be related to iron overload.", "HEPATOPATÍA ALCOHÓLICA:Hepatopatía alcohólica is liver disease caused by excessive alcohol consumption, which can interact with iron overload conditions.", "ANEMIA CON SOBRECARGA FÉRRICA:Anemia con sobrecarga férrica is a type of anemia that occurs in conjunction with iron overload.", "TALASEMIA MAYOR:Talasemia mayor es una enfermedad hereditaria grave que afecta la producción de hemoglobina en el organismo. Esta condición puede requerir tratamientos intensivos, incluyendo trasplantes de células hematopoyéticas. Además, los pacientes con talasemia mayor a menudo necesitan recibir transfusiones de sangre frecuentes, lo que puede resultar en una sobrecarga de hierro en el cuerpo.", "ANEMIA SIDEROBLÁSTICA:Anemia sideroblástica is a type of anemia characterized by the presence of ringed sideroblasts in the bone marrow, often associated with iron overload.", "ANEMIA HEMOLÍTICA CRÓNICA:Anemia hemolítica crónica is a chronic form of anemia that can lead to iron overload due to increased red blood cell destruction.", "ANEMIA APLÁSICA:Anemia aplásica is a condition where the bone marrow fails to produce sufficient blood cells, which can be complicated by iron overload.", "DÉFICIT DE PIRUVATO KINASA:Déficit de piruvato kinasa is a rare genetic disorder that can lead to hemolytic anemia and may be associated with iron overload.", "ACERULOPLASMINEMIA:Aceruloplasminemia is a rare genetic disorder that affects iron metabolism and can lead to iron overload."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}